# --- HARDENED broker: per-topic Access Control List (Phase 2, Control 1) ---
#
# Enforces least privilege: each device may touch ONLY its own topics, in the
# correct direction. This is what defeats the Phase-1 masquerade / spoofing /
# modification attacks at the broker layer — a client authenticated as the
# camera can no longer forge home/frontdoor/lock/state, and no device can
# subscribe to the whole "home/#" tree the way an anonymous client could.
#
# "write" = publish, "read" = subscribe. Order: a per-user block applies to
# that user until the next "user" line. No matching rule => denied.

# Temperature sensor: may only publish its own reading.
user sensor-livingroom
topic write home/livingroom/temperature

# Door lock: publishes its state, and reads commands addressed to it.
user lock-frontdoor
topic write home/frontdoor/lock/state
topic read home/frontdoor/lock/cmd

# Camera: may only publish its own status.
user camera-frontdoor
topic write home/frontdoor/camera/status

# Dashboard (the signed-in human operator): reads the whole home tree for the
# live view, and may send lock commands. It cannot publish device state itself,
# so it cannot spoof a sensor/lock/camera.
user dashboard
topic read home/#
topic write home/frontdoor/lock/cmd
